    equivalent to calling \c{setLocalData(nullptr)}.

    If T is a value type, the stored \c T object is destroyed. This cannot
    be achieved with setLocalData(), which always stores a new value.

    The data of other threads is not affected.

    \sa setLocalData(), hasLocalData(), localData()
*/

